WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.800
Hey guys, House of the Dragon is a Game of
Thrones prequel show that will air in 2022

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.800
on HBO.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.530
It’s based on George RR Martin’s book
Fire And Blood.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.600
The key event of the prequel will be the Dance
of the Dragon, a Targaryen civil war.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:19.330
Although it's a Targaryen civil war, Targaryens
are not the only main characters in this time

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:25.010
period, one major character among them being
Corlys of House Velaryon, known as the Sea

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.420
Snake.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.859
House Velaryon in general plays a key role
in this war.

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:34.290
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:41.500
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.040
I's throne.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.970
Both of them thought they belonged on the
Iron Throne.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:50.910
When people started declaring for one of them
or the other, their fight divided the kingdoms

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.200
in two.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.730
As I already said, the Game of Thrones prequel
series, House of the Dragon, although based

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:02.430
on George RR Martin's Targaryen history book
Fire &amp; Blood, will not feature Targaryens

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:07.819
only, but many other houses and many other
legendary figures from that time period as

00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:13.829
well, including the Velaryons had for centuries
remained the oldest and closest allies of

00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:15.619
the Targaryens.

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:21.119
House Velaryon of Driftmark rules the island
of Driftmark, the largest island of Blackwater

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:22.880
Bay in the crownlands.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.290
Their castle includes Driftmark and High Tide.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:31.060
The head of House Velaryon is titled Lord
of the Tides and Master of Driftmark.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:34.200
The Velaryons are sworn to Dragonstone.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.189
Their arms depict a silver seahorse on sea
green.

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:43.170
Their words do not appear in the books, but
according to semi-canon sources they are "The

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.409
Old, the True, the Brave".

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:50.989
House Velaryon, much like House Targaryen,
is of Valyrian descent, and its members often

00:01:50.989 --> 00:01:55.609
have Valyrian features, such as silver hair
and purple eyes.

00:01:55.609 --> 00:02:01.310
The traditional name of the Velaryons is Jacaerys,
and in House of the Dragon, the main character

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:06.520
Rhaenyra’s oldest son is named Jacaerys,
as his father is from House Velaryon.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:12.299
It’s traditional for the sons of House Velaryon
to be given a taste of a seafarer's life when

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:13.299
young.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:18.180
The positions of master of ships and lord
admiral are often filled by a member of House

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.409
Velaryon, as the family provides most of the
royal fleet.

00:02:22.409 --> 00:02:27.800
House Velaryon is an ancient and proud house,
with the blood of old Valyria in its veins.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:34.329
A noble house with a storied Valyrian lineage,
the Velaryons had come to Westeros even before

00:02:34.329 --> 00:02:39.900
the Targaryens, settling in the Gullet on
the low-lying and fertile isle of island of

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:46.239
Driftmark (so named for the driftwood that
the tides brought daily to its shores) rather

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:49.480
than its stony, smoking neighbor, Dragonstone.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:55.319
The castle of Driftmark housed their ancient
high seat, the Driftwood Throne, which according

00:02:55.319 --> 00:03:00.849
to legend had been given to them by the Merling
King to conclude a pact.

00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:05.530
Although never dragonriders, the Velaryons
had for centuries remained the oldest and

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:08.200
closest allies of the Targaryens.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.290
The sea was their element, not the sky.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.920
During the Conquest, it was Velaryon ships
that carried Aegon’s soldiers across Blackwater

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.680
Bay, and later formed the greater part of
the royal fleet.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:25.730
Throughout the first century of the Targaryen
rule, so many Lords of the Tides served on

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:32.280
the small council as master of ships that
the office was widely seen as almost hereditary.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:38.489
They allied with House Targaryen from Dragonstone
and House Celtigar from Claw Isle, both houses

00:03:38.489 --> 00:03:43.750
of Valyrian descent; while the Velaryons and
Celtigars dominated the middle reaches of

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:49.359
the narrow sea with their ships, the Targaryens
ruled the skies with their dragons.

00:03:49.359 --> 00:03:54.090
The close relations between Houses Velaryon
and Targaryen resulted in multiple marriages

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:59.239
between the houses, both before and after
the Wars of Conquest.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:02.670
Even the mother of Aegon the Conqueror was
a Velaryon.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:07.920
House Velaryon officially allied with the
Targaryens at the start of Aegon's Conquest.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:13.370
Lord Daemon Velaryon was made master of ships
by Aegon the Conqueror after the mouth of

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:16.449
the Blackwater Rush had been secured.

00:04:16.449 --> 00:04:21.620
Daemon died fighting for Aegon I in the battle
in the waters off Gulltown, however.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:26.190
House Velaryon kept an influential position
at the court of the Targaryen kings during

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:29.580
the first two centuries of the Targaryen reign.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:34.060
It even was a Velaryon who became the first
Lord Commander of the Kingsguard for Aegon

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.290
the Conqueror.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:39.840
The most famous and strongest Velaryion to
ever live is also one of the main characters

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:45.099
in the upcoming House of the Dragon show – Corlys
Velaryon, known as the Sea Snake.

00:04:45.099 --> 00:04:50.729
He's a fabled Lord of the Tides during the
Targaryen civil war, Master of Driftmark,

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:52.360
and head of House Velaryon.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:58.330
He is the husband of Princess Rhaenys Targaryen,
the Queen-Who-Never-Was.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:02.610
During the Dance of the Dragons, he became
Hand to Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen who was his

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.759
niece and daughter-in-law.

00:05:04.759 --> 00:05:09.580
By the of age seven-and-thirty, Corlys was
hailed as the greatest seafarer the Seven

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.270
Kingdoms had ever known.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:17.110
Corlys was born in 53 AC to the eldest son
of Lord Daemon Velaryon.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:22.690
He was named after his great-great uncle,
Ser Corlys Velaryon, who served King Aegonthe

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.460
Conqueror as the first Lord Commander of the
Kingsguard.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:32.030
Ser Corlys sailed aboard his Sea Snake, a
ship he designed and built, on nine great

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:34.310
voyages to Essos.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:39.990
During his final voyage on Sea Snake, Corlys
filled the ship's hold with gold and bought

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:45.099
twenty more ships at Qarth, loading them with
spices, elephants, and silk.

00:05:45.099 --> 00:05:50.560
Only fourteen ships made it to Driftmark and
all the elephants died, but it was still more

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:55.120
than enough to make Corlys become the wealthiest
man in all of Westeros.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.410
He took his nickname "Sea Snake" from his
famous ship.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:04.419
SerCorlys became head of House Velaryon and
Lord of the Tides after the death of his grandsire.

00:06:04.419 --> 00:06:10.699
Richer than Lords Lannister or Hightower through
his expeditions, Lord Corlys used his great

00:06:10.699 --> 00:06:16.840
wealth to construct a new seat, High Tide,
where he stored his eastern treasures.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:22.590
In 90 AC, Corlys married the sixteen-year
old Princess Rhaenys Targaryen, the only child

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:28.659
of Prince Aemon Targaryen, who in turn was
the eldest son of King Jaehaerys I Targaryen.

00:06:28.659 --> 00:06:34.560
Two years later, Corlys sailed his fleet to
Tarth, to aid Prince Aemon in fighting the

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.620
Myrish exiles who had invaded the island.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:42.360
Shortly before they left, Corlys's wife announced
she was pregnant.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:47.700
During the campaign, Prince Aemon died, leading
King Jaehaerys I Targaryen to appoint a new

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.700
heir to the throne.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:56.190
He chose his second son Baelon over Aemon's
only heir, Rhaenys, thereby also passing over

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.860
Corlys and Rhaenys's unborn child.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:03.669
Furious over this decision, Corlys gave up
his admiralty and his place on the king's

00:07:03.669 --> 00:07:07.300
small council and returned to Driftmark with
his wife.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:11.659
In late 92 AC,Rhaenys gave birth to a daughter,
Laena.

00:07:11.659 --> 00:07:14.880
A son, Laenor, followed in 94 AC.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:22.229
When Prince Baelon died in 101 AC, King Jaehaerys
I's succession became unclear again, and reports

00:07:22.229 --> 00:07:27.189
reached the court that Corlys was gathering
ships and men to defend the rights of his

00:07:27.189 --> 00:07:28.189
son.

00:07:28.189 --> 00:07:32.729
When the king declared a Great Council would
be held at Harrenhal to settle the succession,

00:07:32.729 --> 00:07:38.470
Corlys and his wife traveled there, using
their wealth and influence to try and persuade

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:43.720
the lords present to vote for Laenor, after
Rhaenys and Laena had been passed over once

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.830
again on account of their gender.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:52.190
Corlys's wealth, reputation and fame did much
to support Laenor's claim, but in the end,

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:58.840
Baelon's son Viserys received majority of
the votes, and was named the Prince of Dragonstone.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:04.530
Following the death of Queen Aemma Arryn,
in 105 AC, Grand Maester Runciter suggested

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:09.949
to King Viserys I Targaryen that he shall
take Corlys's twelve-year-old daughter, Laena,

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:11.090
to wife.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.990
King Viserys, however, chose Alicent Hightower.

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:20.699
Angered by the third time his wife and children
had been scorned by House Targaryen, Corlys

00:08:20.699 --> 00:08:24.439
and his family did not attend the wedding
in 106 AC.

00:08:24.439 --> 00:08:30.330
Instead, he made an alliance with Prince Daemon
Targaryen, King Viserys's younger brother,

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:33.250
equally angered by the King's marriage.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:38.790
Lord Corlys and his fleet fought alongside
Prince Daemon Targaryen during the War for

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.010
the Stepstones.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:45.750
When Daemon declared himself the King of the
Stepstones and the Narrow Sea, Corlys placed

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.870
the crown on the new king's head.

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:54.720
In 113 AC, King Viserys I and his small council
began discussions concerning a betrothal for

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.790
Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen, Viserys's heir.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:01.840
They eventually agreed on Corlys's son, Laenor.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:08.730
Laenor and Rhaenyra were married in 114 AC
and gave him 3 grandsons.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:14.210
By 115 AC, Corlys saw his daughter Laena wed
to Daemon with his blessing.

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:19.280
Through this marriage, Corlys would have two
more grandchildren: the twins Baela and Rhaena

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.420
Targaryen, born in 116 AC.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:28.520
The children of Corlys and Princess Rhaenys
Targaryen both died in 120 AC, Laena Velaryon

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:34.170
from childbed fever and Ser Laenor Velaryon
from a quarrel with a knight which is rumored

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.890
to have been organized by Daemon.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:43.560
Later in the same year Prince Daemon, Laena's
widower, married Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen,

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.560
Laenor's widow.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:51.640
When King Viserys I Targaryen died in early
129 AC, and the King's eldest son Aegon II

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:58.170
Targaryen ascended the throne, passing over
Viserys's appointed heir Rhaenyra, Corlys

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:03.570
traveled to Dragonstone to lend his support
in the struggle to his former daughter-in-law.

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:08.250
Lord Corlys Velaryon sat on the black council
during the civil war known as the Dance of

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:13.380
the Dragons; he was the greatest lord to pledge
his strength to the cause of Queen Rhaenyra

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:19.410
Targaryen, who was opposed by her half-brother,
King Aegon II Targaryen.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:24.080
More than half of Rhaenyra's army was made
of men sworn to House Velaryon.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:27.950
Corlys's fleet also gave the blacks superiority
at sea.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.800
Corlys was Rhaenyra's Hand of the Queen.

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:35.750
When Lord Bartimos advised the princess to
fly from Dragonstone to King’s Landing at

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:42.790
once and reduce the city to ash and bone with
her dragon, Corlys demanded to know how that

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:47.560
would serve them, telling him "we want to
rule the city, not burn it to the ground".

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:52.060
You will see many Velaryons in the House of
the Dragon, with the Sea Snake having the

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:53.540
most screen time, of course.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:59.510
He had served four kings and a queen, sailed
to the ends of the earth, raised House Velaryon

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:06.230
to unprecedented levels of wealth and power,
married a princess who might have been a queen,

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:12.180
fathered dragon riders, built towns and fleets,
proved his valor in times of war and his wisdom

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:13.670
in times of peace.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:17.960
The Sea Snake’s life is so interesting that
there is another Game of Thrones prequel in

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:22.550
development, based on his life alone, called
9 Voyages.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:27.820
Whether you like the Sea Snake and House Velaryon
or you prefer House Targaryen and their dragons,

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:32.710
all of that and more you’ll see in the House
of the Dragon in 2022 on HBO.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:39.250
Thank you so much for watching and stay tuned.

